      "skos:prefLabel": "Backpropagation algorithm",
      "skos:definition": "An algorithm that computes the gradient of a network's loss with respect to every parameter by applying the chain rule backward through the computation, from the output to the inputs, reusing values stored during the forward pass; it is the reverse mode of automatic differentiation specialised to neural networks.",
      "kto:domain": "deep-learning",
      "dcterms:created": "2026-10-31",
      "kto:maturity": "foundational",
